-- test/fixtures/3.7.0-params.lua
-- Every param a fresh Strata 3.7.0 adds, in menu order, separators and
-- groups included (the params norns itself adds before a script are left
-- out): each as {id, t, name} with its default, and for a control its
-- spec's min, max, warp, step, quantum and units, for an option its
-- options, for a number its min and max, for a group its size n, and for a
-- control or number with a formatter the string it shows at its default
-- (`string`). A file param's default under the load's audio folder is
-- written @AUDIO@ in its place. test/unit/params_setup_test.lua compares
-- this build's params with this list: every surviving param keeps its id,
-- default, spec and place (the groundwork before 3.8, its Global
-- Constraints); the differences a later package makes on purpose are listed
-- in that test.
--
-- How it was recorded (2026-11-17): a temporary detached worktree of the tag
-- v3.7.0 (`git worktree add --detach <scratch>/v370 v3.7.0`), a throwaway
-- unit file there that seeds math.randomseed(37), runs h.load_strata() (its
-- before_load noting where the script's params begin) and
-- h.finish_startup(context), and writes each param from that index on, a
-- number as the shortest of "%.15g" to "%.17g" that reads back exactly and a
-- string with "%q"; the string at the default is params:string(id) with the
-- param's value set to its default for the call and put back after. Run
-- with `lua test/run.lua <its filter>` (Lua 5.3.6); LuaJIT 2.1 wrote the
-- same list. The worktree was then removed with `git worktree remove`.
